From 48e825ad7b86bd5c2ec5b133993c9ef83233c710 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marco Meyer-Conde <marco.meyer@glitchr.io>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 13:19:50 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Drell-Yan with a different PDF set for each hadron

A new collider, twoSets, takes hadron 1 from the PDF set the Resummation is
built with and hadron 2 from a second set given with
Resummation::SetSecondHadronPDF(). It covers fixed-target Drell-Yan such as
a pion beam on a nuclear target (pi- W for E615 and NA10), where the two
hadrons have nothing in common. alpha_s and the quark masses stay those of
the first set. pp, ppbar and pd are unchanged.

The second set reaches lumi_DY through the Lum_inclusive/Lum_rapidity
helpers; a twoSets collider without a second set aborts.

example_DrellYan: -2/--pdf-set2 <set> selects it.

Check: twoSets with the same set on both sides reproduces the pp run to all
printed digits (M = 6 GeV, Y = 0.3, sqrt(s) = 21.7 GeV: Delta K = 0.117788,
0.0524331, 0.0142503).
